{% ctaSection
   heading="Program Overview"
   description="The BOLD Program is a gap year program for graduated high school seniors through recent college graduates (or age 19-24). It is aimed at equipping individuals to become more like Christ while immersing them into “real life” experiences as they better discover who they are as an adult and pursue future career paths. Examples of ways in which participants will engage the world around them include balancing an external job, being involved in a local church, serving at camp, setting a personal budget, paying off debts and reaching personal goals that shape them more into the image of our Creator. A primary goal of this program is to equip, mentor, and build confident men and women to serve as Student Leaders during our Summer Camps between June and July. Through intentional spiritual formation, shared community, and hands-on skill development, participants will prepare to enter the next phase of life grounded in faith, ready to guide the future generations into a transformative way of living."
   variant="brown"
   external=false %}
